Version: @VERSION@
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Maintainer: Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>
Homepage: https://biblio.livtet.olamaelcu.net
Depends: nodejs (>= 22), adduser
Recommends: postgresql
Description: Bibliograph catalog worker (provider hydration and PDS outbox)
 The long-running graphile-worker process behind Bibliograph. It enriches the
 catalog from Google Books, ISBNdb and Goodreads, and drains
 public.pds_outbox into the publisher PDS with
 com.atproto.repo.applyWrites.
 .
 The payload is plain ESM with its production dependencies (graphile-worker,
 pg) deployed beside it at /usr/lib/bibliograph-worker, so it runs on the
 host's nodejs with no pnpm or build toolchain. Configuration lives in
 /etc/bibliograph/worker.env.
 .
 Without publisher credentials (PDS_URL, a publisher DID, and an app password
 or provisioned access token) hydration still runs, but pds-publish is
 disabled and says so at boot; catalog rows stay queued in pds_outbox.
